# ─── Supabase / Prisma Connection ──────────────────────────────────────────
# DATABASE_URL: Pooled runtime connection (pgBouncer via Supabase pooler).
#   Used by Prisma client at runtime — supports many concurrent short-lived
#   connections efficiently through connection pooling.
# DIRECT_URL: Direct (non-pooled) connection for Prisma migrations and seeding.
#   Bypasses pgBouncer — required because DDL operations need a direct session.
# ─── Supabase Auth (browser-safe) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL: The Supabase project API URL. Prefixed with
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_ so it is available in the browser for the Supabase JS client.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY: The Supabase "anon" (publishable) key.
#   Browser-safe — this key has limited permissions enforced by RLS policies.
# ─── Supabase Auth (server-only) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY: The Supabase "service_role" (secret) key.
#   Server-only — this key bypasses RLS and must NEVER be exposed to the
#   browser or committed with a real value. Used for admin operations
#   (e.g. creating auth users from the seed script).
DATABASE_URL=
DIRECT_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
